 2026, 7:49 PM EDT\n\n| Market Cap | 26.86B -38.2% |\n| --- | --- |\n| Revenue (ttm) | 4.67B +0.4% |\n| Net Income | 1.48B -4.4% |\n| EPS | 1.55 -2.5% |\n| Shares Out | 926.38M |\n| PE Ratio | 18.71 |\n| Forward PE | 17.85 |\n| Dividend | n/a |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | n/a |\n\n| Volume | 10,152,107 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Open | 28.89 |\n| Previous Close | 29.09 |\n| Day's Range | 28.61 - 29.18 |\n| 52-Week Range | 25.72 - 45.26 |\n| Beta | 1.06 |\n| Analysts | Buy |\n| Price Target | 39.00 (+34.48%) |\n| Est. Earnings | Nov 19, 2026 |\n\n## About CPRT\n\nCopart, Inc. provides online auctions and vehicle remarketing services in the United States, the United Kingdom, Germany, Brazil, Canada, the United Arab Emirates, Spain, Finland, Oman, the Republic of Ireland, and Bahrain. The company provides a range of services to process and sell vehicles over the internet through its virtual bidding third generation internet auction-style sales technology. It offers services, such as online seller access; salvage estimation; estimating; end-of-life vehicle processing; transportation; vehicle inspection sta... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Specialty Business Services\n\nSector Industrials\n\nIPO Date Mar 16, 1994\n\nEmployees 11,900\n\nStock Exchange Nasdaq\n\nTicker Symbol CPRT\n\nWebsite https://www.copart.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn fiscal year 2026, Copart's revenue was $4.67 billion, an increase of 0.41% compared to the previous year's $4.65 billion. Earnings were $1.48 billion, a decrease of -4.39%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 12 analysts, the average rating for CPRT stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $39.0, which is an increase of 34.48% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $39.0 (34.48% upside) Analyst Consensus: Buy\n\n### Copart Proxy statement: Proxy filing\n\n### Copart Proxy statement: Proxy filing\n\n### Midday Fly By: Oracle reports ‘beat and raise,’ Copart to buy ACV Auctions\n\nThe major averages were sharply higher near noon, curtailing some of this week’s declines after four straight down sessions. The rebound comes as oil prices retreat roughly 3% from their…\n\n6 weeks ago - TheFly\n\n### Why is ACV Auctions Stock (ACVA) Motoring 44% Higher Today?\n\nShares in ACV Auctions ($ACVA) accelerated 44% in pre-market trading after agreeing to be bought by peer Copart ($CPRT) for $1.9 billion. The price of $10.50 a share represents a…\n\n### Copart upgraded to Outperform from Market Perform at Barrington\n\nBarrington analyst Gary Prestopino upgraded Copart (CPRT) to Outperform from Market Perform with a $40 price target after the company released Q4 results and announced that it will be acquiring…\n\n6 weeks ago - TheFly\n\n### Oracle, Adobe, Copart, RH, Chevron, and More Stocks That Explain Today's Market\n\nShares of Oracle rise after the software giant's first-quarter results help ease some concerns about its reliance on OpenAI.\n\n6 weeks ago - Barrons\n\n### Copart price target lowered to $38 from $42 at Baird\n\nBaird lowered the firm’s price target on Copart (CPRT) to $38 from $42 and keeps an Outperform rating on the shares. The firm updated its model following quarterly results which…\n\n6 weeks ago - TheFly\n\n### CCC Intelligent Solutions edges lower after Copart agrees to acquire ACV\n\nShares of CCC Intelligent Solutions (CCC) edged lower in after-hours trading after Copart (CPRT) agreed to acquire ACV Auctions (ACVA) for $10.50 per share in cash. The Fly notes that…\n\n### Copart Earnings Call Transcript: Q4 2026\n\nRevenue grew modestly in Q4 and FY26, with international segments showing strong double-digit growth while U.S. volumes declined. Announced the acquisition of ACV to enhance digital capabilities and buyer liquidity, with the deal expected to be accretive in FY28. Liquidity remains strong, supporting ongoing investments and future M&A.\n\n### Copart Earnings release: Q4 2026\n\nCopart released its Q4 2026 earnings on September 10, 2026, summarizing the period's financial r