) Stock Price & Overview\n\n# Verisk Analytics, Inc. (VRSK)\n\nNASDAQ: VRSK · Real-Time Price · USD\n\n195.88 -7.45 (-3.66%) Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT - Market closed\n\n| Market Cap | 25.49B -23.2% |\n| --- | --- |\n| Revenue (ttm) | 3.14B +5.0% |\n| Net Income | 885.50M -3.3% |\n| EPS | 6.50 +0.2% |\n| Shares Out | 130.16M |\n| PE Ratio | 30.15 |\n| Forward PE | 23.99 |\n| Dividend | $2.00 (1.02%) |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | Sep 15, 2026 |\n\n| Volume | 2,019,432 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Open | 203.00 |\n| Previous Close | 203.33 |\n| Day's Range | 192.60 - 204.19 |\n| 52-Week Range | 155.94 - 237.85 |\n| Beta | 0.69 |\n| Analysts | Buy |\n| Price Target | 226.47 (+15.62%) |\n| Earnings Date | Nov 5, 2026 |\n\n## About VRSK\n\nVerisk Analytics, Inc. engages in the provision of data analytics and technology solutions to the insurance industry in the United States and internationally. The company offers underwriting solutions, including forms, rules, and loss costs services that provides policy language, prospective loss costs, policy writing and rating rules, and underwriting solutions for risk selection and segmentation, pricing, and workflow optimization; underwriting data and analytics solutions, which provides property and auto specific rating, and underwriting in... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Consulting Services Sector Industrials IPO Date Oct 7, 2009 Employees 8,000 Stock Exchange Nasdaq Ticker Symbol VRSK Website https://www.verisk.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn 2025, Verisk Analytics's revenue was $3.07 billion, an increase of 6.63% compared to the previous year's $2.88 billion. Earnings were $908.30 million, a decrease of -5.21%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 19 analysts, the average rating for VRSK stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $226.47, which is an increase of 15.62% from the latest price.\n\n### Global Insured Catastrophe Losses Now Expected to Average $171 Billion Annually, Verisk Finds\n\nJersey City, N.J., Sept. 01, 2026 (GLO